# ⚠ THIS FILE DOES NOTHING ON THE CURRENT HOST.
#
# The site is published on GitHub Pages, which serves no custom response headers. Every rule below
# is therefore INERT. It is kept, rather than deleted, because it is the specification of what this
# site needs the day it moves to a host that can serve headers — and because §26 is explicit that an
# absent control must be DECLARED, never left implied: an absent control looks exactly like a site
# that never needed one.
#
# WHAT IS ACTUALLY MISSING, AND WHAT WAS RECOVERED
#
# Recovered from inside the document, in the <head> of every page:
#   Content-Security-Policy   — as a <meta http-equiv>, minus the directives meta cannot carry
#   Referrer-Policy           — as <meta name="referrer">
#
# NOT recoverable, and live on the site right now as gaps:
#   frame-ancestors           — ignored in a meta policy. THE SITE HAS NO PROTECTION AGAINST BEING
#                               FRAMED. On a page giving medical information that is the one that
#                               matters: a third party can present this doctor's advice as its own.
#   X-Content-Type-Options    — cannot be expressed in markup at all.
#   Permissions-Policy        — cannot be expressed in markup at all.
#
# Strict-Transport-Security is served by GitHub Pages itself once "Enforce HTTPS" is enabled on the
# custom domain, so that one is covered by the host rather than by this file.
#
# All of this is recorded in brief.md under the hosting decision, with what would reverse it.

# Response headers — Handbook §26.
#
# These are the controls a static site has NOWHERE ELSE to put. On a host that cannot serve custom
# headers this file does nothing, and the section is explicit about the consequence: no enforceable
# content policy, and NO PROTECTION AGAINST FRAMING AT ALL, because frame-ancestors cannot be
# expressed from inside the document. That is a reason to choose a different host, not a reason to
# proceed quietly.
#
# Syntax below is the edge-host format used by Cloudflare Pages and Netlify. See the banner above
# for what happens to it on the host actually in use.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  # frame-ancestors is the one that cannot be done in markup. This is why the header layer matters.
  # This site is a medical practice: being framed inside somebody else's page is how a visitor ends
  # up believing a third party is the one giving the clinical advice.
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'none'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com; connect-src 'self' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com
  # NOTE: 'unsafe-inline' in script-src is what a tag container requires without a nonce, and a
  # static site cannot mint a nonce per request. This is a REAL WEAKENING and it is recorded rather
  # than hidden — see brief.md, "Assumed and accepted".
  #
  # `form-action 'none'` rather than the usual 'self': this site presents no form at all, so any
  # submission attempt is either an injection or a mistake. Restore it to 'self' the day a form is
  # added, and add its receiver's origin.

# Markup revalidates. A wrong address, matriculation number or scheduling link stays live for
# exactly the cache lifetime, and some hosts have no purge at all.
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Corrected last, so never cached long.
/robots.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
/sitemap.xml
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
/llms.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

# Versioned in the URL from config.assetVersion, so these are safe to freeze.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
